# freecam-corpus.manifest - (level, pose) tuples for the debug-freecam golden.
#
# One row per pose:  <level> | pos=(x, y, z) yaw=Y pitch=P | [start]
#   level  a --skip-to-level name (artisans, cliff_town, gnorc_cove, ...)
#   pose   a freecam pose string (the exact per-tick freecam log format;
#          the game extracts the 5 integers, so paste it verbatim; an
#          optional "roll=N" after it rolls the view, absent = 0)
#   start  optional pinned canonical frame (default 1900; +50 = intermediate).
#          Raise it for a level that loads slower than the default post-load frame.
#
# Each pose is captured native-only at 16:9, both LOD modes, on two legs
# (canonical + alpha-0.5 intermediate). Verify each first sample
# renders real geometry (not a load/transition frame) before blessing.
