# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Portal-sky / arch boundary cases.
#
# Where the destination-sky preview meets the arch is the hardest edge in the
# renderer: the PSX confines the preview by OT painter order plus a scissor
# rect, and a depth buffer has to reproduce that silhouette from depth and a
# stencil aperture instead. Every failure below is a different way that
# reconstruction goes wrong, and each is ANGLE-dependent - an arch viewed
# square-on hides all of them, because the defects live on the jamb that
# recedes away from the camera. Hence exact poses.
#
# Two invariants these rows exist to protect:
#   1. The sky must not appear anywhere outside the arch opening.
#   2. The preview's junction with the ground must be a STRAIGHT LINE.
#      (PsyCross itself gets #2 wrong sometimes, so it is not the arbiter
#      here - straightness is judged directly.)
#
# NOTE these are captured at both LOD modes by the corpus driver, which
# matters: the distant-arch row below only misbehaves under extended LOD,
# where the arch renders at a range the original would have culled.

# Sky escaping PAST the arch - the preview paints over the stone jamb and the
# wall behind it. Cause: the sky's rect spill carried one constant depth (the
# farthest outline point), but on an angled arch the jamb OUTSIDE the opening
# recedes past that depth and loses to it. Broken = a purple/blue wedge sitting
# on the stone at the upper LEFT, growing as yaw turns the far side away.
dream_weavers | pos=(31259, 44935, 13693) yaw=1379 pitch=-66
# Close on a portal opening with a waterfall directly behind it: the preview
# fills the frame and the waterfall's ABR-1 faces sit inside the outline. Guards
# the blended-terrain portal cover discard (portal_cover_scene.glsl) - the preview
# draws depth-test-only, so without it the additive pass blends over the preview.
dream_weavers | pos=(73050, 69383, 13760) yaw=-1400 pitch=41
# Close on a portal at a sheer angle, where the arch silhouette cuts the opening.
# Guards the flat/dome coverage identity on INTERMEDIATE presents: the stencil
# mask is the outline dilated by the aperture margin while the dome is confined
# to a rect, so a band can exist that only the flat reaches. Canonically the
# stone hides it; sub-tick the silhouette shifts and it shows as a bright sliver.
# The corpus's `inter` leg is what catches this - the canon leg cannot.
dream_weavers | pos=(72461, 66230, 13605) yaw=-2567 pitch=67
# Far back from a portal arch (d=32000), where the arch's sector has handed its
# HP tier over to LP. Guards the per-face scoping of the LP depth pull: applied
# to every LP face the pull is proportional, so at this range it exceeds the
# ~40 units by which the arch clears the opening plane and the plane-pinned
# preview eats a face-sized bite out of the jamb. Original-LOD leg is the one
# that matters - under extended LOD the HP never drops and there is no LP here.
dream_weavers | pos=(108122, 83001, 15311) yaw=-1794 pitch=9

# Gap between the preview and the arch INTERIOR at close range. Cause: clipping
# the sky strictly to the authored outline polygon under-covers - the outline
# sits inside the visible opening. Broken = a dark sliver down the inner jamb,
# between the stone and the preview.
beast_makers | pos=(120326, 113108, 18243) yaw=-509 pitch=79

# The same edge at DISTANCE (needs the extended-LOD leg). Opposite sign to the
# row above and the reason a single global margin is not sufficient: here the
# outline IS the visible opening, so widening the aperture opens a dark band
# along the inner edge that grows with the margin. A change that fixes the
# close arch by widening must be checked here before it is believed.
beast_makers | pos=(111382, 124004, 17636) yaw=3474 pitch=-14

# Sky/ground junction, straightness invariant (#2). Broken = the junction
# breaks into a staircase, because the sky fill was pushed below the sill into
# ground that is nearer and lost the depth test along terrain triangle edges.
beast_makers | pos=(119196, 113801, 17840) yaw=-669 pitch=246

# Ground junction, PRE-EXISTING defect (present with the portal aperture
# disabled, and NOT introduced by it). The terrain under the opening bulges up
# into the preview in a curved hump instead of meeting it flat - the terrain
# OT-conformance sink failing to flatten those faces to the sky plane. Kept as
# a row so the eventual fix has a witness; expect it to look wrong today.
beast_makers | pos=(118535, 113493, 16946) yaw=3397 pitch=104

# Portals whose ARCH GEOMETRY ANIMATES, and which any coplanar-geometry rule
# must skip: the arch is a dragon head that stretches, portal included, as it
# opens, so the opening plane moves with the mesh and geometry that is not the
# static inner rim can go momentarily coplanar with it. By destination levelId:
# 14 (artisans -> toasty) and 62/63/64 (gnorc_gnexus -> twilight_harbor /
# gnasty_gnorc / gnastys_loot). This is NOT "boss portals" - doctor_shemp(24),
# blowhard(34), metalhead(44) and jacques(54) are ordinary static arches.
#
# artisans -> sunny_flight(15) is a different case and is NOT excluded: a wall
# lowers to reveal it, but the arch mesh itself never changes. Only its capture
# timing matters - a shot taken right after the level loads frames the wall.

# Inner rim coincident with the preview. Rims are present on every arch EXCEPT
# beast_makers/tree_tops(43) and gnorc_gnexus/gnorc_cove(61); dream_weavers
# authors its rims visible from ONE SIDE only (51/52/53 detect from the near
# side, 54/55 from the far), so an empty result from one side is correct there.
# Broken = shimmer along the inner rim as the camera moves.
peace_keepers | pos=(73452, 77502, 55889) yaw=2942 pitch=81

